1. Dataset Summary
What is the dataset about?
The dataset contains information about gamers and their gaming behavior, along with demographic, financial, health, lifestyle, addiction, and productivity-related information.
The main objective of analyzing this dataset is to understand:
How gaming behavior and gaming addiction are associated with players' lifestyle, mental-health indicators, spending behavior, and productivity.
________________________________________
What type of information does the dataset contain?
The dataset can broadly be divided into five categories.
1. Demographic information
This includes variables such as:
•	Age
•	Gender
•	Country
•	Occupation
•	Years of gaming
•	User/player information
These variables help us understand who the players are.
________________________________________
2. Gaming behavior
The dataset contains information related to:
•	Daily playtime
•	Weekend playtime
•	Gaming platform/device
•	Preferred gaming genre
•	Behavioral cluster
•	Addiction score
•	Addiction severity
•	Addiction status
These variables help identify how players interact with gaming.
________________________________________
3. Financial / monetization information
The dataset also contains:
•	Monthly spending
•	Revenue-related information
•	Lootbox openings
•	Gaming-related spending behavior
This allows us to analyze the financial side of gaming behavior.
________________________________________
4. Health and lifestyle information
The dataset contains indicators such as:
•	Sleep hours
•	Social interaction hours
•	Exercise frequency
•	Loneliness score
•	Stress score
•	Anxiety level
•	Dopamine dependency index
These variables allow us to examine the relationship between gaming behavior and lifestyle/mental-health indicators.
________________________________________
5. Productivity-related information
There are also variables such as:
•	Productivity drop percentage
•	Absenteeism days
These help analyze the potential impact of gaming behavior on productivity and regular responsibilities.
____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________
In this project, I first cleaned and transformed the dataset using Power Query and prepared the data for analysis.
I created DAX measures to calculate important KPIs such as Total Players, Addiction Rate, Average Age, Average Addiction Score, Total Revenue, Average Monthly Spending and Productivity-related metrics.
I then created three dashboard pages covering Player Demographics, Financial Insights, and Health, Productivity & Risk Assessment. I used different visualizations such as KPI cards, bar charts, column charts, donut charts, matrix tables and scatter plots to identify patterns and relationships.
I also added slicers and filters for interactive analysis and used conditional formatting to highlight high and low values. Finally, I organized the visuals into a clear dashboard layout so that the insights could be easily understood."

In short, the work I did was:
- Data cleaning & transformation — Power Query
- Data modeling — organized fields/relationships as required
- DAX measures — KPIs and analytical calculations
- KPI cards — overall performance indicators
- Charts & visualizations — demographic, financial, health and productivity analysis
- Matrix/table — behavioral cluster and mental-health comparison
- Conditional formatting — highlighted high/low values
- Slicers — Country, Occupation and other interactive filtering
- Scatter plots — analyzed relationships such as addiction vs productivity and playtime vs spending
- Dashboard design — organized the project into 3 focused pages
- Insights — interpreted patterns and associations rather than just displaying numbers
